            "text": "{\"primary_meaning\": \"The vulnerable, defenseless, and marginalized in society who are under God's special protection, often representing humanity's helpless spiritual state without God.\", \"primary_basis\": [\"Psalm 68:5\", \"James 1:27\", \"Deuteronomy 10:18\", \"Exodus 22:22\"], \"alternatives\": [{\"meaning\": \"The spiritual state of disciples or humanity without Christ's presence or the Father's adoption.\", \"basis\": [\"John 14:18\", \"Romans 8:15\"], \"prominence\": \"common\"}, {\"meaning\": \"A broad prophetic metonymy for all victims of systemic societal injustice and oppression.\", \"basis\": [\"Isaiah 1:17\", \"Jeremiah 5:28\", \"Zechariah 7:10\"], \"prominence\": \"common\"}], \"has_settled_consensus\": true, \"confidence\": \"high\", \"notes\": \"In biblical literature, the fatherless are frequently grouped with widows and aliens to represent those lacking the traditional economic and legal protection of an adult male patron, serving as a primary test of Israel's covenant faithfulness and a reflection of God's character as a defender of the weak.\"}",
